# Every layer of the exit stack assumed 16:00 close — holiday early-close days were a blind stack, not a single missed check

## Symptom

`FABLE-FULL-AUDIT-2026-09-01.md` §4 item 2 / line 158: verified against the live broker
calendar, 2026-11-27 and 2026-12-24 close at 13:00 ET. On either date a 0DTE opened before
13:00 has no automated exit before it expires; an ITM contract auto-exercises into ~$77K of
stock per contract. Invisible in paper (no physical settlement in paper trading).

## Root cause

Not one missed check — a STACK of independent components each hardcoding a 16:00 close and
none of them calendar-aware:
- `heartbeat_core._is_rth` = `weekday()<5 and 9.5<=h<=16.0` (first line of `main()`, no
  calendar lookup at all).
- Entry cutoffs (09:35/15:00) and the time stop (15:40) are fixed wall-clock values.
- `Gamma_EodFlattenCore`/aggressive flatten fire at fixed 15:52/15:55.
- Task Scheduler triggers are plain Mon-Fri with no holiday/early-close exception.
- `engine_health.market_is_open()` IS holiday-aware (built after the 2026-07-03 incident)
  but is never called by the trading engine itself, and its own cache discards the `close`
  field it fetches — so even the one component that knew the right answer threw it away
  before anything could read it.

## Fix

Commit `4683f05e` (2026-09-01), task B2 — flatten half shipped without touching any frozen
file: `setup/scripts/market_calendar.py` (new shared writer); `calendar.json` now persists
`early_closes:{date:'HH:MM'}` alongside `holidays[]`; `eod_flatten.py --only-if-early-close`
+ new task `Gamma_EodFlattenEarlyClose` (weekdays 12:32 ET) checks today's close (cached,
live `/v2/calendar` GET fallback), NOOPs on a normal 16:00 day, **fails CLOSED** (no action)
if calendar state is unknown either way, and sweeps identically to the Core flatten once
`now_et >= close-30min` on a genuine early close. `engine_health.py` gained a non-critical
`early_close_today` visibility check. 10 tests, RED-proofed (threshold 30->5 min fails).
**Entry-cutoff half still open** — `_is_rth`/09:35 entry gate/15:40 time stop going
calendar-relative lives inside frozen `heartbeat_core.py`; tracked as queue item
`EARLY-CLOSE-CALENDAR-AWARENESS`, HARD DEADLINE before 2026-11-27.

## Generalizable pattern

A time-based assumption ("market closes at 16:00") baked independently into N components
is N separate bugs, not one — fixing the flatten side does not fix the entry-cutoff side,
and a component that "already knows better" (`market_is_open()`) is worthless if nothing
calls it or if it discards the field the caller would need. Audit for this pattern: grep
every fixed-clock constant (`16.0`, `15:40`, `09:35`) against whether it has a calendar-
relative alternative available and wired.
